    "slug": "somali-journalist-dies-from-wounds-after-baidoa-shooting-nusoj-calls-for-probe",
    "summary": "Bashir Mohamed Abdullahi, a 23-year-old reporter with Arlaadi Media Network, died on September 7 from injuries suffered in a shooting in Baidoa four days earlier. The National Union of Somali Journalists (NUSOJ) is urging authorities to investigate and hold those responsible accountable.",
    "content": "A young journalist in Somalia has succumbed to injuries sustained during a security incident in the southwestern city of Baidoa. Bashir Mohamed Abdullahi, a reporter for Arlaadi Media Network, died in the early hours of Monday, September 7, according to the National Union of Somali Journalists (NUSOJ). He was 23 years old.\n\nThe shooting occurred on September 3 in the Al-Ahmaar neighborhood in northern Baidoa. At the time, clashes were taking place between government forces and militias aligned with Abdiaziz Hassan Mohamed, also known as Laftagareen, the former leader of South West State. Local journalists informed NUSOJ that Abdullahi was at his home when the violence erupted and that he sustained critical gunshot wounds.\n\nNUSOJ has expressed deep sorrow over the loss and is calling for a thorough investigation into the circumstances surrounding his death. The union emphasizes that journalists must be protected under both national and international law, and it urges Somali authorities to ensure that those responsible for the killing are brought to justice.\n\nThe incident highlights the ongoing risks faced by media workers in Somalia, particularly in regions affected by political and military tensions. For the Somali diaspora, this tragedy underscores the importance of press freedom and the need for accountability in the homeland, as many diaspora members rely on local journalists for reliable news and often advocate for stability from abroad.",
