    "summary": "Relatives of 10 Pakistani fishermen held hostage by Somali pirates since April 2026 staged a protest in Karachi, urging the Pakistani government to speed up their release. The crew members were part of the MT Honour 25, captured near Puntland.",
    "content": "In Karachi, Pakistan, family members of ten Pakistani crew members from the oil tanker MT Honour 25 have taken to the streets, demanding urgent government action to secure the release of their loved ones. The crew members have been held hostage by Somali pirates for over four months, since their vessel was seized on April 21, 2026.\n\nThe MT Honour 25, flying the Palau flag, was en route when it was captured in waters off the coast of Puntland, a semi-autonomous region in northeastern Somalia. The hijacking occurred under unclear circumstances, but the pirates have maintained control of the crew and vessel since then, marking nearly 140 days of captivity.\n\nThe protesting families in Karachi have expressed deep frustration, noting that they have had no communication with the captives for about a month and a half. They are calling on the Pakistani government to intensify diplomatic and operational efforts to negotiate the crew's freedom, emphasizing the prolonged separation and the deteriorating conditions of their relatives.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, this incident highlights the persistent security challenges in the Horn of Africa, which not only affect regional stability but also impact international maritime routes. Many diaspora members have ties to both regions, and such events underscore the need for collaborative solutions to combat piracy, which has economic and human costs reaching far beyond Somalia's shores.\n\nThe Pakistani government has yet to respond publicly to the families' protest, but the urgency of the situation is clear. The crew members' safety remains uncertain, and the families' plight reflects a broader humanitarian concern that the international community, including the Somali diaspora, must not overlook.\n\nRead the original report from Goobjoog here: https://goobjoog.com/2026/09/07/qoysaska-badmaaxiinta-pakistan-ee-afduubka-loogu-haysto-soomaaliya-oo-dalbanaya-xorriyaddooda/",
